{"id": "8e48189a-6c46-442e-880e-5d429f09f601", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"text": "Now let me gather the read-only data needed to assess where things stand — this touches several AWS APIs (RDS, ElastiCache, DynamoDB, AWS Backup, Resilience Hub, networking), so I'll pull it together in the background rather than filling your chat with raw API output.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "tooluse_hA82hpm6ekpDqkSrmYOuJI", "tool_name": "gather_context", "input": {"prompt": "{
  "task": "Gather read-only AWS data to assess disaster recovery (DR) readiness for an application backend workload in eu-central-1. The workload's named resources are: an RDS (or Aurora) MySQL instance/cluster named 'dr-demo-mysql', an ElastiCache Valkey replication group named 'dr-demo-valkey', and a DynamoDB table named 'dr-demo-players'. All calls must be read-only (Describe/List/Get only). Do not create, modify, or delete anything.",
  "context": "User wants a disaster recovery assessment covering four failure scenarios: single service failure, single AZ failure, Region failure, and bad data (accidental delete/bad deploy). They have not yet defined RPO or RTO targets. I (the chat agent) will write the final report myself using this raw data — return DATA ONLY, do not write a prose summary or recommendations.",
  "resources": ["dr-demo-mysql (RDS/Aurora MySQL)", "dr-demo-valkey (ElastiCache Valkey replication group)", "dr-demo-players (DynamoDB table)", "eu-central-1 region"],
  "timeframe": "current state, not time-bounded",
  "criteria": "Run these checks in eu-central-1, all read-only:\n\n1. WORKLOAD BOUNDARY: Check whether this workload is already registered in AWS Resilience Hub next-gen (resiliencehubv2) via ListServices (match by name/resources); if found, also call GetService, ListResources, GetPolicy, ListFailureModeFindings. Separately, find any additional resources belonging to the same workload beyond the 3 named ones: cloudformation:ListStacks/ListStackResources, tag:GetResources (look for tag keys like app/application/service/project/workload, especially anything tagged or named with 'dr-demo'), servicecatalog ListApplications (AppRegistry). Report any compute (EC2/ECS/EKS/Lambda), entry/routing (ALB/NLB/API Gateway/CloudFront/Route53), or messaging resources connected to this workload.\n\n2. RDS/Aurora (dr-demo-mysql): rds:DescribeDBInstances (MultiAZ, Engine, BackupRetentionPeriod, ReadReplicaDBInstanceIdentifiers, DeletionProtection, StorageEncrypted, AvailabilityZone). If Aurora, also DescribeDBClusters and DescribeGlobalClusters. DescribeDBInstanceAutomatedBackups (any replicated automated backups in another region). DescribeDBSnapshots (manual/automated, and their region).\n\n3. ElastiCache (dr-demo-valkey): elasticache:DescribeReplicationGroups (member/replica count, AutomaticFailover, MultiAZ, SnapshotRetentionLimit, GlobalReplicationGroupInfo, node type, EngineVersion). DescribeSnapshots.\n\n4. DynamoDB (dr-demo-players): dynamodb:DescribeContinuousBackups (PointInTimeRecoveryStatus, RecoveryPeriodInDays). ListBackups (on-demand backups). DescribeTable (Replicas field — is it a global table? If DescribeTable is denied, fall back to DescribeContinuousBackups/ListBackups only and note replica info couldn't be read).\n\n5. AWS Backup: backup:DescribeRegionSettings (check ResourceTypeManagementPreference.DynamoDB flag for advanced features), ListBackupPlans, ListProtectedResources, ListRecoveryPointsByResource for all 3 resources (do recovery points actually exist, not just plan membership). If any copy rules target another region, check ListRecoveryPointsByBackupVault on the destination vault and ListCopyJobs to see if copies actually landed.\n\n6. Network / shared dependencies for the AZ-failure scenario: which VPC/subnets do these resources use, how many AZs do they span, ec2:DescribeNatGateways and DescribeRouteTables (zonal vs regional NAT), ec2:DescribeVpcEndpoints (AZ coverage). Also check KMS (are the RDS/DynamoDB resources encrypted, is there a key, is it a multi-region key) and Secrets Manager (any secrets tied to this workload, and whether they have replica regions via DescribeSecret).\n\n7. For every check, note explicitly if a call was denied or returned empty so I can label it 'not checked' vs 'no gap found'.\n\nReturn results as DATA ROWS using this exact format, one row per resource: layer | resource | type | Region | in-Region redundancy (AZs, nodes, tasks) | backups (kind, frequency, retention) | copies, images or IaC outside the Region | point-in-time recovery | replication | what could not be read. Also separately report: (a) Resilience Hub registration status and findings if registered, (b) any additional workload resources/boundary discovered beyond the 3 named ones, (c) network/shared-dependency findings, (d) a list of any denied/skipped calls."
}"}, "type": "tool_use", "display_intent": "Gather read-only DR posture data for MySQL, Valkey, DynamoDB workload in eu-central-1"}], "created_at": null}
